<title>CANADA: IBM Canada names Wetmore as president, CEO.</title>
<headline>IBM Canada names Wetmore as president, CEO.</headline>
<dateline>MARKHAM, Ontario 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>IBM Canada Ltd said on Tuesday it named John Wetmore as IBM Canada's president and chief executive, replacing Khalil Barsoum, who was appointed chairman and chief executive of IBM United Kingdom.</p>
<p>Wetmore was most recently president and chief executive of ISM Information Systems Management Corp, a wholly-owned unit of IBM. Succeeding Wetmore in that position is Normand Bourassa, who was vice-president of IBM Quebec.</p>
<p>IBM said Barsoum was also named chairman of IBM Canada replacing William Etherington, who was named general manager of IBM Europe, Middle East and Africa.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
